    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d33">

                <pb facs="0152" n="134" sameAs="frus:frus1951v06p1/pg134"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">790.5/1–451</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by Mr. John Foster Dulles, the Consultant to
                        the Secretary, to the Ambassador at Large</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Jessup</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d33-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1951-01-04">January 4, 1951</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In order to facilitate the discussion of a possible Pacific Ocean Pact set for
                    11:00 a. m., January 5, I have prepared the annexed comment on the draft already
                    circulated.</p>


                <xi:include href="d33-a1.xml" xpointer="d33-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d33-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d33-f1-content">
                <p>Memorandum addressed also to Messrs. Matthews, Rusk, Fisher, Nitze, Labouisse,
                    Allison, and Emmerson.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
